WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:19.701
"We're not supposed to use magic unless absolutely necessary," Maff told Zann and his friends.

2
00:00:19.721 --> 00:00:22.223
"We'd better walk to the dungeon."

3
00:00:22.243 --> 00:00:25.906
"Who banned magic inside the palace?"

4
00:00:25.926 --> 00:00:26.567
Zann asked.

5
00:00:27.688 --> 00:00:28.588
"I'm not sure."

6
00:00:29.049 --> 00:00:30.109
Maff looked troubled.

7
00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.652
The ban sounded strange to Zann.

8
00:00:33.672 --> 00:00:36.855
With the king and queen gone, who was in charge at the palace?

9
00:00:37.836 --> 00:00:39.697
Normally it would be the Red Council.

10
00:00:40.178 --> 00:00:42.099
But why would they ban magic?

11
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.001
It didn't make sense.

12
00:00:48.885 --> 00:00:51.487
A huge guard stood outside the dungeon's entrance.

13
00:00:52.608 --> 00:00:54.650
He wasn't dressed like the other palace guards.

14
00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.372
His uniform was entirely black.

15
00:00:57.392 --> 00:00:58.733
"Who are you?"

16
00:00:59.153 --> 00:01:00.274
Maff asked the guard.

17
00:01:00.294 --> 00:01:02.056
"Why are you dressed like that?"

18
00:01:02.816 --> 00:01:04.517
The guard ignored Maff's questions.

19
00:01:05.237 --> 00:01:06.198
"What's your business here?"

20
00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:06.918
he demanded.

21
00:01:06.938 --> 00:01:09.840
"I want to see my parents," Zann said.

22
00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.061
"They're in the dungeon."

23
00:01:12.041 --> 00:01:13.682
The guard looked him up and down.

24
00:01:13.702 --> 00:01:17.664
"Go ahead," he said, stepping aside to let them pass.

25
00:01:17.684 --> 00:01:20.086
"But don't use any magic."

26
00:01:25.048 --> 00:01:28.210
"That's odd," Maff said as the group walked down the steps.

27
00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.252
"That guard wasn't wearing a typical uniform.

28
00:01:32.112 --> 00:01:33.412
I wonder what's going on."

29
00:01:34.473 --> 00:01:36.353
Zann spotted more guards below.

30
00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:39.034
They were dressed just like the guard upstairs.

31
00:01:39.874 --> 00:01:42.535
Zann pushed past them, eager to see his family.

32
00:01:42.555 --> 00:01:45.096
"Zann!" his father exclaimed.

33
00:01:45.116 --> 00:01:46.696
"What are you doing here?"

34
00:01:46.716 --> 00:01:48.477
"We wanted to see you."

35
00:01:48.797 --> 00:01:49.897
Zann hurried closer.

36
00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.978
His mother was in the cell next to Nax.

37
00:01:53.518 --> 00:01:54.818
Boz and Teplo were nearby.

38
00:01:54.838 --> 00:01:56.899
"Uncle Gar!"

39
00:01:57.219 --> 00:01:58.379
Gliss cried suddenly.

40
00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:00.520
"How did you end up in there?"

41
00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.282
Zann quickly scanned the cells.

42
00:02:04.102 --> 00:02:06.404
Gliss' uncle was right beside Teplo.

43
00:02:07.384 --> 00:02:09.526
Other members of the Red Council were locked up too.

44
00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:12.668
"I don't see Venna," Perda whispered.

45
00:02:13.409 --> 00:02:15.890
She shot a careful glance at the nearest guard.

46
00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.752
"Or Saffa," Zann murmured back.

47
00:02:18.772 --> 00:02:19.753
"That's good."

48
00:02:20.554 --> 00:02:25.377
The scene reminded Zann of the time when Morb had imprisoned most of the Reds in Magica.

49
00:02:26.138 --> 00:02:29.320
But Morb wasn't doing this, or someone would have seen him.

50
00:02:30.176 --> 00:02:32.177
The thought made Zann feel a little better.

51
00:02:32.937 --> 00:02:33.757
But only a little.

52
00:02:34.777 --> 00:02:38.639
How could he talk to his parents and the others with all these guards listening?

53
00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.820
Maff seemed to be thinking the same thing.

54
00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.240
"May we have a moment of privacy?"

55
00:02:44.541 --> 00:02:45.581
he asked the guards.

56
00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:48.302
"The boy wishes to speak with his parents."

57
00:02:49.282 --> 00:02:52.303
"Sorry," a guard said, not sounding sorry at all.

58
00:02:52.323 --> 00:02:54.043
"We have our orders.

59
00:02:54.404 --> 00:02:55.404
We must stay."

60
00:02:56.424 --> 00:02:58.566
Maff opened his mouth as if to argue.

61
00:02:58.846 --> 00:03:00.708
But Zann's mother leaned forward.

62
00:03:00.728 --> 00:03:03.590
"It's all right, kids," Asta said.

63
00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:07.173
"It's good to see you, but you don't need to worry about us."

64
00:03:07.193 --> 00:03:10.135
"That's right," Uncle Gar added.

65
00:03:10.155 --> 00:03:13.077
"This will all get sorted out after Venna is elected."

66
00:03:13.098 --> 00:03:15.720
"Just stay safe, all right?"

67
00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:16.680
Nax said.

68
00:03:17.481 --> 00:03:20.844
Before Zann could answer, footsteps pounded down the stairs.

69
00:03:23.144 --> 00:03:26.906
All the guards spun around and saluted as Laddno stepped into the room.

70
00:03:26.926 --> 00:03:30.028
"At ease, fellows," he told the guards.

71
00:03:30.969 --> 00:03:36.472
His hands clasped behind his back, he strolled toward the cells, ignoring Maff and the kids.

72
00:03:36.492 --> 00:03:39.254
"Hello, citizens," he said.

73
00:03:39.274 --> 00:03:42.375
"I'm sorry to see you in such dire straits."

74
00:03:43.336 --> 00:03:44.417
"Hmph," Boz said.

75
00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:46.238
Nobody else made a sound.

76
00:03:47.218 --> 00:03:49.780
Laddno wandered up and down the row of cells.

77
00:03:50.756 --> 00:03:54.639
"I wish to inform you that your happiness is very important to me," he said.

78
00:03:54.659 --> 00:04:00.344
"If you are all innocent, as you claim, I'll make sure you're released once I've been elected king."

79
00:04:00.364 --> 00:04:03.546
"Why not release them now?"

80
00:04:03.807 --> 00:04:04.908
Perda said boldly.

81
00:04:04.928 --> 00:04:09.331
"Nobody seems to be in charge now that the king and queen have disappeared.

82
00:04:09.872 --> 00:04:13.735
I bet you and Venna could join together to free the prisoners right away."

83
00:04:14.876 --> 00:04:16.116
Laddno peered at her.

84
00:04:16.137 --> 00:04:17.438
"Who are you?"

85
00:04:17.758 --> 00:04:18.238
he asked.

86
00:04:19.179 --> 00:04:21.032
"Never mind her," Boz said.

87
00:04:21.052 --> 00:04:22.873
"We're okay, kids.

88
00:04:23.373 --> 00:04:25.133
We can wait until after the election."

89
00:04:25.813 --> 00:04:27.194
"Yes," Teplo added.

90
00:04:27.214 --> 00:04:30.675
"But if you're worried, you should recite my favorite poem.

91
00:04:31.715 --> 00:04:33.836
It's called 'Ode to a Turnip.'"

92
00:04:34.276 --> 00:04:35.216
He cleared his throat.

93
00:04:35.236 --> 00:04:39.557
"Such a fine fruit, ah!

94
00:04:40.077 --> 00:04:42.798
Happiness attends the chewing herewith."

95
00:04:43.678 --> 00:04:44.979
Laddno scowled at him.

96
00:04:44.999 --> 00:04:47.299
"Enough with the poetry," he snapped.

97
00:04:47.819 --> 00:04:49.420
"I never could stand that nonsense.

98
00:04:49.896 --> 00:04:50.857
What's the point of it?"

99
00:04:50.877 --> 00:04:53.419
"What's the point, indeed?"

100
00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.322
Teplo beamed at him and then winked at Zann.

101
00:04:56.342 --> 00:04:58.364
"Now, be off with you.

102
00:04:59.064 --> 00:05:01.727
Children and turnips both require fresh air, hmm?"

103
00:05:03.108 --> 00:05:05.710
Zann exchanged confused looks with his friends.

104
00:05:06.991 --> 00:05:09.073
Teplo had always been a little strange.

105
00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:11.936
Had prison finally made his mind snap?

106
00:05:12.877 --> 00:05:13.557
"You heard the man."

107
00:05:13.857 --> 00:05:15.359
Laddno gestured to the guards.

108
00:05:15.379 --> 00:05:16.520
"Take them outside."

109
00:05:18.824 --> 00:05:21.646
Zann was soon outside the palace walls with his friends.

110
00:05:22.286 --> 00:05:23.067
"Where's Maff?"

111
00:05:23.327 --> 00:05:23.947
Perda asked.

112
00:05:23.967 --> 00:05:25.708
"I'm not sure."

113
00:05:26.048 --> 00:05:27.069
Zann looked around.

114
00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:31.832
The guards had zapped them outside, but Maff was nowhere in sight.

115
00:05:31.852 --> 00:05:34.013
"I guessed he stayed in the palace."

116
00:05:34.874 --> 00:05:35.534
"I've got it!"

117
00:05:35.674 --> 00:05:36.555
Darb blurted out.

118
00:05:37.235 --> 00:05:38.356
The others stared at him.

119
00:05:38.376 --> 00:05:40.517
"What?" Gliss asked.

120
00:05:40.537 --> 00:05:42.018
"The poem."

121
00:05:42.298 --> 00:05:43.118
Darb grinned.

122
00:05:43.138 --> 00:05:45.440
"I know what Teplo was trying to tell us."

123
00:05:46.408 --> 00:05:50.210
Zann had already almost forgotten about that silly turnip poem.

124
00:05:50.831 --> 00:05:52.552
"What are you talking about?"

125
00:05:52.572 --> 00:05:55.453
"It's an acronym," Darb explained.

126
00:05:55.473 --> 00:06:06.159
"The first letters of each word of the poem are Perda gasped.

127
00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.681
"Saffa hatch!"

128
00:06:08.941 --> 00:06:09.581
she exclaimed.

129
00:06:09.601 --> 00:06:14.024
"That must mean that Saffa is hiding out in the hatch at Teplo's house."

130
00:06:15.132 --> 00:06:18.215
"She must be afraid she'll be taken prisoner too," Zann said.

131
00:06:18.235 --> 00:06:21.018
"And Teplo wants us to hide with her!"

132
00:06:21.178 --> 00:06:21.798
Darb added.

133
00:06:21.818 --> 00:06:26.122
"Shh." Zann glanced around, hoping nobody had heard them.

134
00:06:26.683 --> 00:06:28.204
He didn't want to wind up in prison.

135
00:06:28.224 --> 00:06:30.146
"What are we waiting for?"

136
00:06:30.346 --> 00:06:30.847
Gliss said.

137
00:06:30.867 --> 00:06:32.168
"Let's go!"

138
00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:36.332
All was quiet at Teplo's house.

139
00:06:37.193 --> 00:06:39.355
Zann checked to make sure nobody was nearby.

140
00:06:43.788 --> 00:06:46.749
Then he knocked on the hatch outside the front door.

141
00:06:47.749 --> 00:06:50.850
It creaked open, but there was no other sound.

142
00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:53.111
"Should we go down?"

143
00:06:53.311 --> 00:06:54.971
Gliss asked, sounding nervous.

144
00:06:54.991 --> 00:06:56.732
"I'll go first."

145
00:06:57.532 --> 00:06:58.912
Zann tried to look brave.

146
00:06:59.873 --> 00:07:03.534
He sat down on the edge and lowered himself into the darkness below.

147
00:07:03.554 --> 00:07:10.316
Abruptly he let out a scream—his entire body was engulfed in flames!
